  "resource": "res_light",
  "job": "Draws a caught ally back to the group; when he falls low, nobody beside him can be touched for a breath.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "lore": "Sukri walks the rim of the dial with a staff over his shoulder and a glass cup of noon light hanging from its crook. He has been walking so long that the cup has grown warm and the staff has grown thin. He keeps the habit of the Hourless: carry what you can for whoever needs it, and never ask whose side they are on. When someone near him falls behind, the cup swings and the road gets shorter. When he falls behind himself, the people around him have learned to stand very still and let the light sort it out.",
